# 🌐 Networking

## VPC Building Blocks
- **VPC** — isolated virtual network (e.g., `10.0.0.0/16`)
- **Subnet** — CIDR range within a VPC, tied to one AZ
- **Internet Gateway (IGW)** — enables internet for public subnets
- **NAT Gateway** — outbound-only internet for private subnets
- **Route Table** — rules directing traffic
- **Security Group** — stateful instance firewall
- **NACL** — stateless subnet firewall

## Public vs. Private Subnet
| Feature | Public | Private |
|---------|--------|---------|
| Route to IGW | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |
| Auto-assign public IP | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |
| Reachable from internet | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |

## CIDR Cheatsheet
| CIDR | Addresses | Usable (AWS) |
|------|-----------|--------------|
| /24 | 256 | 251 |
| /23 | 512 | 507 |
| /16 | 65,536 | 65,531 |

> AWS reserves 5 addresses per subnet.
